# Long /faction threads about PvE, social life and the economy that fit any realm. Realm-specific
# places come from slots ({capital}, {zone}, {camp}, {dungeon}); no realm's towns, zones or classes
# are named. Topics are period knowledge from the research brief, written as new lines.

@kind debate
@realm *

@topic camp_etiquette
@levels 15-40
@scene soc_camp_dispute
@role B type=Leveler
@role C type=Socialite
@role D type=Daredevil
@role E type=*
A: {q} is there a rule about camps or is it just whoever is fastest | so someone just walked into {camp} and started pulling our spawn
B: if you were there first its your camp, everyone knows that | first come first served, always has been
A: i told them that. they said they didnt see us
C: didnt see a whole group sitting in a circle? lol | eight people sitting in a ring and they didnt see us. sure
B: some people really dont check. ask them to group up | send them a tell, half the time they just want xp too
?D: or just out-pull them, whoever tags it first gets it
B: thats how a camp turns into a mess
~ 25
A: update, sent a tell, they said they were camping it yesterday | ok they replied. apparently it was their camp last night
C: yesterday doesnt count. you leave, you lose it
E: unless they left a buddy sitting there to hold it | did they leave someone holding it? thats the only exception i know
A: nope, nobody
D: then its yours. keep pulling and let them get bored | then pull faster and smile
?E: i held a camp for a guildie once while they ate dinner, nobody argued
C: thats different, a body sitting at the camp is a claim
~ 40
A: ok they joined us. they were a solid tank actually | well. they joined the group. and they can tank. weird ending
B: told you, most ks fights end in a group invite
C: or in a grudge that lasts a month | or in somebody's ignore list forever
D: lol both are valid outcomes
E: whats the tank's name, we could use one tomorrow | add them to your friends list, good tanks are rare at this level
A: will do. pull is up, back later | gotta go, theyre pulling already

@topic train
@levels 10-45
@scene soc_train_story
@role B type=Leveler
@role C type=Socialite
@role D type=NoLifer
@role E type=Explorer
A: TRAIN to the zone line, sorry everyone | train coming out of {dungeon}, move!
B: who is training at this hour | not again
C: we had just sat to med, it went right through us | it ran straight through our camp, we picked up a pile of adds
A: i know, i know. the pull went wrong and the healer died first
B: did you yell before or after you ran
A: before! i yelled in say and in faction
D: yelling only works if people are looking at chat | nobody reads chat mid-fight though
~ 30
C: ok we survived, barely. two of us dead | we lost our puller and our healer, the rest made it
A: i owe you a rez | coming back to rez, give me a sec
?C: you are forgiven if you bring the rez
E: worst train i ever saw was a whole room following one runner across a zone | i once watched a train chase someone all the way to the guards
B: running to the guards is the only good train | the guards are the best part, they eat the whole thing
E: only if the guards are tough enough, some just fall over too
~ 35
D: there should be a rule. if you train someone you owe them a favor | new rule, whoever trains a camp buys the next round of potions
A: deal. i will pay up in {capital} | fair. find me in {capital} later
C: i accept payment in coin lol
?E: whats the going rate for one train, asking for a friend
A: everyone back up? trying that pull again, slowly this time | all rezzed, back to it
B: from the far side this time please
A: from the far side, promise
D: you said that last time too | heh

@topic boat_and_walks
@levels 10-45
@scene soc_boat_walk
@role B type=Socialite
@role C type=Leveler
@role D type=Explorer
@role E type=Crafter
@role F type=Daredevil
A: on the boat again. this ride is so long | {q} anyone else on the boat right now
B: boat rides are the best time to make a sandwich | perfect time to grab a snack
C: or to read faction chat lol | thats when faction gets the most chatter
A: where is everyone headed
D: the shrouded isles, finally old enough for it | heading to the islands for the first time
?B: enjoy, the first trip out there feels huge
~ 30
E: long walks are worse. at least the boat drives itself | walking across a whole zone with no speed buff, now that is pain
C: that is why everyone loves a speed class | a speed class is worth their weight in gold
E: or the horse routes. buy a ticket, go make dinner | stablemaster tickets, the original autopilot
A: ever fallen asleep on a horse route?
F: woke up at the end of the route with something chewing on me | yes. woke up next to a guard staring at me
~ 35
D: whats the best view you have seen on a long trip | best sight anyone has seen on the road?
F: first time i saw the frontier from a distance, those huge keep walls | the first time i saw a keep out there. i just stopped and stared
B: same. i was way too low to be there, i just wanted to look
E: you look, then something with a red name looks back | and then a stealther introduces himself
?F: i died a moment later. totally worth it
C: the water at night from this boat is up there too | the sunset over the sea on this crossing, honestly pretty
A: ok we are docking. back to work | land! finally. off to find a camp
D: good luck everyone on the islands | see you on the other side

@topic ninja_loot
@levels 20-50
@scene soc_ninja_loot
@role B type=Socialite
@role C type=Leveler
@role D type=Daredevil
@role E type=NoLifer
@role F type=*
A: just had someone ninja a drop from our group and leave | someone grabbed the named's drop and disbanded right after
B: what was it
A: a {item} | the thing we had been camping all evening
C: wow. what was the loot rule | did you agree on rolls before the pull?
A: we said roll for it. they just picked it up and left
D: name them in faction | post their name, everyone should know
B: careful with that, sometimes its an accident | could be a misclick, it happens
A: and then disband in the same second? sure
~ 30
E: word gets around. a ninja looter has trouble getting groups for months | people remember this stuff. good luck to them finding a group later
C: our guild keeps a list. not public, just for us
?D: everyone has a list
B: has anyone actually sent them a tell?
A: yes. no answer. probably logged
~ 40
F: hey i know that player, they were in my group last week, very nice | i grouped with that name before, they seemed fine?
A: well they were not nice tonight
F: i will ask them about it, maybe there is a reason
E: there is never a reason that makes that ok
?F: their little brother plays on the account sometimes, i am not kidding
D: lol the little brother defense | ah, the classic little brother
~ 25
F: ok they answered me. they will meet you in {capital} and hand it back | they say sorry, they thought it was free loot, will hand it back
A: well. that is not how i expected this to end | huh. ok. did not see that coming
C: faith in people restored, partly | ok faith restored a little
B: see, send a tell first, post names second

@topic pickup_groups
@levels 15-45
@scene soc_pug_vs_guild
@role B type=Leveler
@role C type=Socialite
@role D type=Crafter
@role E type=Explorer
@role F type=*
A: do you all group with strangers or wait for guildmates | {q} pick up groups or guild groups, which do you prefer
B: guild every time. i know who will stay and who will afk
C: strangers. half my friends list started as a random invite
B: and the other half are names you never want to see again
C: thats what the ignore list is for | lol fair
~ 25
D: my guild is three people and one of them only plays saturdays | small guild here, if i wait for guildmates i wait all week
E: the best groups i had were complete strangers who clicked | my best group ever was eight strangers at {camp}
?E: we kept that group together for a week, every night
A: what happened after
E: two of them made a guild together, the rest scattered | someone moved to an alt and it fell apart
~ 30
B: thats the thing, strangers are a gamble. guildies are a promise
D: a promise to show up an hour late lol | a promise that comes with drama
C: and guildmates can be bad too, you just cant say it | at least with a stranger you can leave, with a guildie you have to be polite
B: ok that is true
?F: i just answer whoever says lfm first
F: honestly the game is better when you take a chance | half the fun is meeting people
A: ok, posting lfg then, see who bites | fine, i will try a random group tonight
C: pst me if nobody bites

@topic midnight_healer
@levels 20-50
@needs night
@scene soc_midnight_healer
@role B type=NoLifer
@role E type=Leveler
A: lf healer, anyone, its late and we are stuck | any healer awake? we have a full camp and nobody to keep us up
B: every healer in the realm went to bed an hour ago
A: at this point i will take anything with a heal spell
B: i can heal a bit, but i am a hybrid with a tiny heal | i have a small heal. it is a small heal. a very small one
A: a small heal is more than we have now | we will take it, any heal helps
~ 30
B: night groups are always like this, everyone rolls damage | and then everyone wonders why there are no healers at night
?B: i rolled a healer once. the tells never stopped, i rerolled
E: im up, but im leveling my alt. what level is your camp | my main is a healer but im on my alt right now
A: low 30s, {camp}
E: ugh, my healer is way past that. greys
B: come anyway, we wont tell anyone | you could just come heal for fun, no xp though
E: heal for no xp at this hour. what a pitch | sell it harder lol
~ 35
A: we will share the loot, all of it | you get first pick on every drop
E: ...ok, the loot offer is tempting
A: and every rez you need, promise | rezzes too, guaranteed
B: buying healers with loot, the oldest trade in the game
E: fine, swapping chars, give me a few | logging over. if i fall asleep at the keyboard dont be mad
A: you are a hero | best person in the realm
?B: nobody tell my guild i was the backup healer
@needs

@topic failed_crafts
@levels 25-50
@scene soc_craft_fails
@role B type=Crafter
@role C type=Crafter,Socialite
@role D type=NoLifer
@role E type=Leveler
@role F type=Crafter
A: failed the same combine over and over tonight | so many fails in a row on one piece, is that normal
B: welcome to crafting | thats a normal tuesday for a crafter
C: what tier are you making, maybe its too high for you
A: right at my skill. it should not fail this much
D: it feels rigged but its not. probably. | everyone says it is rigged. nobody can prove it
~ 25
B: every fail is coin down the drain, thats the real pain | its not the fail, its watching the materials vanish
E: this is why crafted gear costs what it costs
?F: and people still haggle like we pick it off trees
C: i quit crafting after a night like that | i put my crafter on the shelf after a night like that
B: and came back a week later right
C: ...yes
~ 35
A: ok it worked. and its a 99 | finally a success. 99 quality. of course | lol it worked. 99%. so close to masterpiece it hurts
D: 99 is the cruelest number in the game
B: sell it as basically masterpiece | list it as nearly perfect and smile
E: people pay well for a 99, honestly | a 99 sells, just not for masterpiece money
A: going to keep it for myself, i earned it
F: spoken like a true crafter | the crafter's curse, you keep the best ones
?D: describe it to me in detail, i want to feel your pain
A: back to the forge, still need the gloves | ok, gloves next. pray for me

@topic legendary
@levels 30-50
@scene soc_legendary_chase
@role B type=Socialite
@role C type=Leveler
@role D type=NoLifer
@role E type=Daredevil
@role F type=Crafter
A: ding legendary!!! | {q} i finally hit legendary on my crafter
B: GZ!!! | gratz, that is a long road
C: how long did that take you
A: dont ask. i stopped counting the hours | months. i stopped counting at some point
D: how much coin did it eat | do you even want to know what it cost
A: i dont want to know, and i dont want my guild to know
~ 30
E: so you take orders now? i need a full set | open for orders? my guild will flood you
A: give me a day to breathe lol
C: what does legendary even change, honestly
B: better odds of masterpiece, and bragging rights | the masterpiece chance goes up, and people start sending tells
?C: and your name gets known in the capital
D: is it worth it though, when you could have bought the suit
A: no. yes. i dont know. it felt amazing | not in coin. in feeling, absolutely
~ 40
F: congrats from a crafter stuck way below that | i am ages away from that, gz
F: any tips for the long middle?
A: never craft tired, and never look at your coin total | buy materials in bulk, and keep a friend in faction to cheer you on
E: and dont stop when you hit the boring stretch | the middle stretch is where crafters quit. push through
B: first masterpiece out of your forge, show us | make something nice for yourself first
A: first one goes to my guild leader, promised it ages ago
?D: and the second to me, right
A: lol no | not a chance

@topic overcharge
@levels 35-50
@scene soc_overcharge_gamble
@role B type=Crafter
@role C type=Socialite
@role D type=Daredevil
@role E type=Leveler
@role F type=Crafter,NoLifer
A: overcharging a piece, wish me luck | about to overcharge my chest piece. hold me
B: how far over are you going | how greedy are we feeling tonight
A: a little over. not crazy
C: a little over is how it starts | that is what everyone says right before the boom
~ 20
A: it blew up | BOOM. gems gone. | and... it exploded. all the gems
D: lol rip | ouch. pour one out
E: thats why i never overcharge, plain and simple
C: and your stats are a little worse forever
E: and i sleep at night
~ 30
F: who was your spellcrafter, you or a hired one | did you craft it yourself or pay someone
A: myself. so i only have myself to blame | i did it myself. no one to blame
F: some crafters redo it if theirs explode, worth asking around | a few spellcrafters cover blown gems, ask before you pay
B: the honest ones do. the rest shrug | not all of them. some just say risk is risk
?D: i paid for a redo once, still cheaper than starting over
~ 25
A: buying new gems now. trying again | ok, round two, same piece
C: you are insane | admirable. also insane
E: overcharge addiction is real
A: it worked! | IT HELD!!! | success!!! it held
D: gz! now never do that again | gz, quit while you are ahead
A: next piece is the helm... | the helm is next. dont tell me the odds
?B: we will be here for the explosion

@topic dyes_alchemy
@levels 15-50
@scene soc_dye_colors
@role B type=Socialite
@role C type=Crafter
@role D type=Daredevil
