@topic exchange_prices
@levels 20-50
@scene soc_exchange_undercut
@role B type=Socialite
@role C type=Leveler
@role D type=Crafter
@role E type=NoLifer
@role F type=Crafter,Explorer
A: someone undercut my listing on the exchange by one copper | listed something on the realm exchange, undercut within the hour lol
B: welcome to the market | that is the market, it never sleeps
C: just sell to a merchant, no stress
A: merchants pay nothing though | merchant pays a fraction, no thanks
C: a fraction now beats nothing next week
~ 30
D: the trick is listing right before the evening crowd logs on | list in the evening, more buyers
E: i always undercut. sorry. its just how it works | i am the undercutter. i admit it.
A: so it was you lol
E: maybe. what were you selling
A: nope, not telling you now | not saying, you will undercut me again
?B: lol smart
F: the real money is in stuff people burn through, potions, arrows | sell what people need every night. arrows, potions, dye
D: rare drops sit for days though, only a few people can use them
~ 35
C: i still say merchants are underrated, no listing, no waiting
F: and no profit lol | and nothing to brag about either
B: depends. a full bag at a natural break, merchant. one good item, exchange | junk at a break goes to a merchant. anything nice goes to the exchange
A: ok that is a decent rule
E: and if you see me undercut you, just undercut me back | race you to the bottom
A: no thanks, i will relist tomorrow | not playing that game. relisting later
?D: smart. patience wins the exchange

