@topic guild_leader_quits
@levels 25-50
@scene soc_gl_quit
@role B type=Socialite
@role C type=Daredevil
@role D type=NoLifer
@role E type=Leveler
@role F type=*
A: our guild leader just quit the game. gave lead to whoever was online | {q} our gl quit tonight, no warning
B: oof. who got it | ouch. who is in charge now
A: me. i was the only officer online | me, apparently. i was online
C: congrats and sorry | gz? or condolences, not sure which
D: happened to my old guild too. half of us left within a month | when ours quit, the guild split in two by the weekend
~ 30
A: there is already drama about who gets officer
E: give it to whoever actually shows up, simple | ranks go to people who show up. not friends of friends
?D: and keep the loud ones away from the rank list
F: did they say why they quit
A: work, a new job. said real life caught up | something about a new baby, cant blame them
F: thats fair, good for them | can not argue with that
~ 35
B: you could run it like a council. three officers, no single boss | try a council, nobody can blame just you
C: councils argue more | three leaders, three opinions, one guild chat on fire
E: just do a guild night once a week, keeps people together | one fixed night a week. the people who come are your guild
A: thats a good idea actually | guild night. writing that down
?C: do it on a night with no relic raid lol
D: and post something nice for the old leader, they earned it
A: yeah. they founded this thing | already did, everyone signed it in guild chat
B: you will be fine. you care, that is most of the job | you will do fine, the worried ones are always the good ones

